<page>
<exercise workspace = "8in">
<statement>
    <p>
      Let's use the moment generating function technique to find the mean and
      variance:
    </p>
</statement>
</exercise>
</page>
<page>
    <p>
      In Summary:
    </p>

    <p>
      If <m>X</m> is <m>b(n,p)</m>, then
      <md>
        E[X] = \mu = np,\,\,\, Var(X) = np(1-p) = npq; \,\,\, \sigma = \sqrt{npq}
      </md>
    </p>

    <p>
      Note: We will use <m>q</m> and <m>1-p</m> interchangeably.
    </p>

 <exercise>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      Jerry sells life insurance over the phone. The probability of any given
          phone call resulting in a sale is <m>0.1</m>. Suppose Jerry calls
          <m>25</m> people, let <m>X</m> be the number of sales (assume independence
          of the calls).
    </p>
  </introduction>
  <task workspace="1in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        How is <m>X</m> distributed (i.e., write <m>X \sim b(n,p)</m> for
                the correct <m>n</m> and <m>p</m> )?
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
  <task workspace = "0.75in">
    <statement>
      <p>
         How many sales can Jerry expect to make?
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
  <task>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      For each of the following, first write the answer in terms of
                <m>P(X\leq k)</m> (or <m>1-P(X \leq k)</m>, etc.). Then find the
                answer.
    </p>
  </introduction>
  <task workspace = "0.75in">
  <statement>
    <p>
      What is the probability he makes no more than <m>1</m> sale?
    </p>
  </statement>
  </task>
  <task workspace = "0.75in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        At least <m>1</m>?
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
  <task workspace = "0.75in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        Exactly <m>5</m>?
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
  </task>             
  </exercise>
</page>
<page>
  <exercise>
    <introduction>
      <p>
        The probability that the field goal kicker on a certain football team will
          make the field goal is <m>0.80</m>. Assume that each attempt is
          independent. In practice one day the kicker attempts <m>20</m> field
          goals. Let <m>X</m> be the number that are successful.
      </p>
    </introduction>
      <task workspace = "0.75in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            How is <m>X</m> distributed?
          </p>
          </statement>
      </task>
      <task workspace = "0.75in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            What is the expected number of field goals?
          </p>
          </statement>
      </task>
      <task workspace = "0.75in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            What is the probability that exactly <m>12</m> field goals are made?
          </p>
          </statement>
      </task>
      <task workspace = "0.75in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            What is the probability that more than <m>19</m> field goals are
                made?
          </p>
          </statement>
      </task>
      <task workspace = "0.75in">
        <statement>
          <p>
           What is the probability that he misses more than <m>1</m> field goal?
          </p>
          </statement>
      </task>
  </exercise>        
</page>
