<exercise>
    <introduction>
        <p>
            For each of the following, first write the problem as <m>f(x), F(x), </m> or <m> 1-F(x)</m>. 
            Then use you calculator or app to find the answer. 
            Use the format given in class to show work for calculator formulas.
        </p>
    </introduction>
<task workspace="0.75in">
<statement>
    <p>
       For <m>X\sim b(10,0.45)</m> find <m>P(X \leq 2)</m>.  
    </p>
</statement>
</task>
<task workspace="0.75in">
<statement>
    <p>
         For <m>X\sim b(15, 0.3)</m> find <m>P(X\lt 10)</m>.
    </p>
</statement>
</task>
<task workspace="0.75in">
<statement>
    <p>
         For <m>X\sim b(5,0.1)</m> find <m>P(X \geq 2)</m>.
    </p>
</statement>
</task>
<task workspace="0.75in">
<statement>
    <p>
          For <m>X\sim b(20,0.5)</m> find <m>P(X=15)</m>.
    </p>
</statement>
</task>
<task workspace="0.75in">
<statement>
    <p>
         For <m>X\sim b(15,0.9)</m> find <m>P(10 \lt X \leq 13)</m>.
    </p>
</statement>
</task>
<task workspace="0.75in">
<statement>
    <p>
        For <m>X\sim b(15,0.9)</m> find <m>P(10 \leq X \lt 13)</m>.
    </p>
</statement>
</task>
</exercise>
</page>
<page>
    <exercise workspace = "2in">
    <statement>
        <p>
            Your favorite cereal (Sugar-O's) is offering one of four prizes in each box of cereal. There is a <m>0.25</m> probability in each box (assume independence) that 
            the prize will be the secret decoder ring. What is the fewest number of boxes of cereal you need to buy so that the probability
            of getting at least one secret decoder ring is greater than <m>0.5</m>?
        </p>
    </statement>
    </exercise>

    <exercise workspace = "3in">
    <statement>
        <p>
             A hospital obtains <m>40\%</m> of its flu vaccine from Company <m>A</m>, <m>50\%</m> from Companuy <m>B</m>, and <m>10\%</m> from Company <m>C</m>. From past experience, it is known that <m>3\%</m> of the vials from <m>A</m> are ineffective, <m>2\%</m> from <m>B</m> are ineffective, and <m>5\%</m> from <m>C</m> are ineffective. The hospital tests five vials from each shipment. If at least one of the five is ineffective, find the conditional probability of that shipment's having come from <m>C</m>.
        </p>
    </statement>
    </exercise>
</page>
</worksheet>